Several venues have also experienced panic-motivated shopping event which led to empty shelving of essential products such as food, toilet paper, bottled water, including a shortage of supplies.
The technology industry in particular has been warning of delays in the shipping of electronic products.
According to WHO Director-in--Child-General Tedros Adhanom, the demand for personal protective steak rose 100-fold.
“This demand has led to an increase in prices of up to twenty-fold the normal price and has also induced delays in providing medical items for four to six months.
