chloroquine and hydroxylychlorochloroquine with or without azithromythronyin have major limitations that have prevented the medical community from adopting these therapies without further further studies. oseltamivir did not inhibit SARS-CoV-2 in vitrothymyomythecin and does not have a well-known function in COVID-19.
Cytokine storm may be a complication in the later stages of severe COVID-19.
Hydroxychloroquine may have anti-storm properties of cytokine. Tocilzumab has been included in the treatment guidelines by China’s National Health Commission after the completion of a small study.
It is currently underway a non-randomized test in phase 2 at national level in Italy, after having demonstrated positive results in people with severe disease.
Combined with serum ferritin blood test to identify cytokine thunderstorms, it is expected to neutralize these developments, which are considered to be the cause of death of some people affected.
Interleukin-6 receptor antagonist has been approved by the FDA based on retrospective case studies on the treatment of cytokine-replating cytokine refractory to steroid-inducduced causes, CAR T cell therapy in 2017.
So far there is no randomized controlled evidence that tocilzumab is an effective treatment for CRS.
Transgbolized and concentrated antibodies produced by the immunological system who has recovered from COVID-19 for people who in need are being investigated as non-vaccination passive immunization.
This strategy has been tested for SARS with inconclusive results.
Viral Neutralization is an expected mechanism of action whereby passive anti-antibodies therapy can mediate a defense against SARS-CoV2.
Other mechanisms such as anti-occuly cell cytotoxicity and/or phagocytosis may be possible.
Other passive anti-antibode forms of antibogen therapy, such as using manufactured monoclonal antibodies are under development.
Convalescent whey production, which consists of the liquid portion of blood of recovered patients and contains antibodies specific to this virus, could be increased for faster implementation.
